1
2 (a) The affairs of each district shall be
3 administered by a board of directors, each of whom shall be
4 a bona fide resident of Wyoming. Directors for the
5 positions identified in paragraphs (i) and (ii) of this
6 subsection shall be elected at an annual meeting of
7 district livestock owners. Directors for the positions
8 identified in paragraphs (iv) and (v) of this subsection
9 shall be appointed as described. The composition of the
10 board shall be as follows:
11
12 (i) Three (3) directors shall be sheep owners
13 having paid predator management fees on sheep in the
14 district in the year preceding election. At each subsequent
15 annual district meeting one (1) director shall be elected
16 for a three (3) year term, and no director shall serve more
17 than nine (9) years. Subject to the provisions of W.S.
18 11-6-203(a), all sheep owners whether an individual,
19 corporation or partnership, having paid predator management
20 fees on sheep in the district regardless of the domicile of
21 the sheep, are entitled to one (1) vote at the meeting;
22
