1 (ii) Three (3) directors shall be cattle owners
2 having paid predator management fees on cattle in the
3 district in the year preceding election. At each subsequent
4 annual district meeting one (1) director shall be elected
5 for a three (3) year term, and no director shall serve more
6 than nine (9) years. Subject to the provisions of W.S.
7 11-6-203(a), all cattle owners whether an individual,
8 corporation or partnership, having paid predator management
9 fees on cattle in the district regardless of the domicile
10 of the cattle, are entitled to one (1) vote at the meeting;
11
12 (iv) The board of county commissioners shall
13 appoint one (1) director two (2) directors to serve for an
14 initial term of two (2) years and thereafter for three (3)
15 year terms from electors in the county not engaged in
16 raising sheep or cattle. No appointed member may director
17 shall serve for a consecutive period of more than six (6)
18 nine (9) years;
19
20 (v) If the board of directors determines state
21 funds are necessary for an effective predator management
22 program to assure the statutory requirements provided in
23 W.S. 11-6-205 are fulfilled and state funds are
